{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.82,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["Q2", "R2", "U2", "U3", "Q1"],
      "pins": ["Q2.1", "Q2.3", "R2.1", "R2.2", "U2.6", "U3.6", "Q1.1"],
      "nets": ["PWM", "Net-(Q2-B)"],
      "observed": "The MCU PWM pins U2.6/U3.6, the PMOS gate Q1.1, the NPN collector Q2.3, and one side of the base resistor R2.1 are all on net PWM; R2.2 is on Net-(Q2-B), so R2 connects the collector/gate node back to the NPN base.",
      "expected": "For the high-side PMOS switch, the MCU output should drive Q2's base through R2 (MCU -> R2 -> Q2.B), while Q2.C should be the PWM/gate node pulled up by R1; the MCU pin should not be tied to the collector/gate node with R2 forming base-collector feedback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"9\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") ... (node (ref \"Q2\") (pin \"3\") ... (node (ref \"R2\") (pin \"1\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"7\") (name \"Net-(Q2-B)\") (node (ref \"Q2\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"R2\") (pin \"2\") ..."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The PWM node cannot be driven high: when it rises above about 0.7 V Q2 conducts and pulls it down, keeping Q1 on and preventing normal fan PWM/power control; it may also cause excessive MCU pin current/contention.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity around Q2/R2 is anomalous: the MCU and PMOS gate are tied to the NPN collector, and R2 feeds that same node back to the base, creating a clamp/feedback path instead of a base-drive level shifter."
}

